 "ranked_on": "drag_per_dollar - maker fee (both legs fill), the two terms that are measured. Reward density is shown beside the rank, never inside it.",
 "fee_status": "DERIVED FROM VENUE METADATA, not from a paid invoice. GET /series/{ticker} declares fee_type=quadratic and fee_multiplier=1 for all eight series, identical to the certified KXBTC15M/KXETH15M pair.",
 "fee_vs_reward_asymmetry": "A STRUCTURAL ASYMMETRY THAT THE EQUATION HIDES. The maker fee is charged per contract EXECUTED. The liquidity reward is scored on orders RESTING, with no fill required. So the fee term and the incentive term are not incurred by the same event: an order that rests and is never hit earns reward and pays nothing. The fee figure below therefore belongs to the PAIR-MANUFACTURING business (both legs fill), not to the pure liquidity-provision business, and a leg can rank differently under the two. We cannot yet price the second because share of score is unknown.",
 "residual_note": "UNMEASURED on this venue -- we hold no fills here. It is not zero, and it is the term that actually sank PMUS: -6.458%/$ came from unpaired inventory, not pair cost.",
