 "the_tension": "DRAG AND SHARE PULL IN OPPOSITE DIRECTIONS ACROSS LEGS, and this is the reason a series average is worse than useless here. The legs with the CHEAPEST books carry the THICKEST competition near the mid, because cheap books are cheap precisely because many makers are already standing there. The legs with almost no near-mid competition are wide, and you pay that width on every pair you manufacture.\n\nSo there is no leg that is simply 'best'. There is a frontier, and where you want to sit on it depends on which business you are in: pair manufacturing is punished by width, pure liquidity provision is punished by crowding, and the fee falls only on the first of those. Any single ranking that hides this frontier is selling one number where the decision needs two.",
 "share_denominator": "reported as a curve over band width; the venue's proximity rule is unknown to us",
 "shadow_only": true,
 "order_entry": false,
